WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.033
Six Sigma and the Role of Measurement

2
00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:10.466
Welcome to this session as we look at the power of measurement.

3
00:00:10.466 --> 00:00:13.932
In specific, we’re going to take a look at the role of measurement

4
00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:17.399
in this area that we call Six Sigma.

5
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.533
This is a phenomenally important concept

6
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:25.733
where Six Sigma is concerned. We cannot over emphasize

7
00:00:25.733 --> 00:00:29.733
the role of our ability to measure things.

8
00:00:29.733 --> 00:00:34.099
Remember, it was Lord Kelvin told us in 1891.

9
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.100
If we cannot express what we know in the form of measurements,

10
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.100
then our knowledge is of a meager and unsatisfactory kind.

11
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.500
It's that simple. Now,

12
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:50.366
given that we can start to look at the idea that knowledge equals measurement.

13
00:00:50.366 --> 00:00:56.299
In other words, we won't know something until we measure.

14
00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.333
Therefore, knowledge and measurement are interconnected.

15
00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:06.133
Especially, where we start to look at the idea of verifiable knowledge.

16
00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:11.366
In other words, if we see some phenomena happen, like a UFO,

17
00:01:11.366 --> 00:01:17.566
then we have to be able to measure it in order to make it verifiable knowledge.

18
00:01:17.566 --> 00:01:22.199
Otherwise its not really knowledge, unless it's scientifically,

19
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.800
the key there is scientifically verifiable.

20
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:33.766
So as a result of that, if we have some experience Y.

21
00:01:33.766 --> 00:01:37.799
And we have to be able to source trace it,

22
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:43.666
then we need to be able to measure Y and X.

23
00:01:43.666 --> 00:01:47.866
To establish the relationship between Y and X.

24
00:01:47.866 --> 00:01:52.566
For example, considering just a simple scatter diagram,

25
00:01:52.566 --> 00:01:56.866
between the Y variable and the X variable.

26
00:01:56.866 --> 00:02:03.332
We might collect X measurements, Y measurements, and relate those measurements

27
00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:08.166
on a simple scatter diagram to look at the strength of association

28
00:02:08.166 --> 00:02:13.832
between X and between Y.

29
00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:18.133
In this case we see there is a positive relationship.

30
00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:24.733
And we can fit a simple line through here, that's a line of best fit and say this.

31
00:02:24.733 --> 00:02:30.899
If we constrain ourselves to this general range.

32
00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.000
We project up and over.

33
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.766
Then we will get our output within this range.

34
00:02:39.766 --> 00:02:43.699
If we stay X in this range,

35
00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.233
we can see how that projects up and projects over.

36
00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:50.199
Now, the only way that we can make that statement,

37
00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.800
is if we're able to measure X and we're able to measure Y.

38
00:02:54.800 --> 00:03:01.766
To establish the function. Y is a function of X. Without the ability to measure,

39
00:03:01.766 --> 00:03:06.532
we couldn't establish such relationships.

40
00:03:06.533 --> 00:03:11.366
This knowledge is verifiable, it’s repeatable.

41
00:03:11.366 --> 00:03:15.899
We could go out and collect more measurements a second time

42
00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:20.633
and see if the same knowledge results.

43
00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:26.566
As we take progressive measurements and the same knowledge occurs

44
00:03:26.566 --> 00:03:33.266
time, and time, and time again, then we can say that that knowledge is verified.

45
00:03:33.266 --> 00:03:37.466
It’s therefore verifiable because we measure it.

46
00:03:37.466 --> 00:03:44.166
And that is one reason that measurement is so important in the concept of Six Sigma.

47
00:03:44.166 --> 00:03:49.166
Thank you for choosing SSMI.
